Well, and you could make anti-magic traps the most
detested traps in the game just by having them
interact with the PCs inventory, too. That YANI
looks like the first step onto a slippery slope.

Other steps along that slope:

- dropping a potion onto an anti-magic trap turns it
  to uncursed water

- dropping an item onto an anti-magic trap sets its
  enchantment to 0 and its status to uncursed

- walking into an anti-magic trap polymorphs some
  fraction of/all of the magical items in the PC's
  inventory into non-magical items of the same
  category

- walking into an antimagic trap clears the
  enchantment on some fraction of/all of the PC's
  inventory

- walking into an antimagic trap sets the BUC status
  of some fraction of/all of the PC's inventory to
  "uncursed"

That would make an anti-magic trap at once a game
crushing nuisance, and way overpowered. Probably the
community doesn't need those traps to go there.

